## A view on where the market is heading

Tomáš Kamhal, founder of Residata: "The distribution of supply across districts changes slowly — new projects appear where the land is, and in Bratislava that is concentrated in a few areas.

The more interesting comparison is supply against sales. Where a district holds a larger share of sales than of supply, its offer is thinning faster than the city average; where it holds a smaller one, it stays on the market longer.

The achieved price in each district is also the best answer to the question of what a flat in Bratislava costs. The city average is one number for five very different markets."

